as refused because every way to make the system claim arrival here weakens the reactive gate, moves a frozen NAV_INSTRUCT digest, or lands the owner's uncommitted grid_planner.py -- and the owner's uncommitted diff, applied alone, only nudges the same stall 3 cm to 1.4996 m, crossing the same radius by 0.4 mm. COST, written rather than hidden: no_authority_disagreement disabled as a kill channel from this re-run; re-armed when D-15 agrees again. A check already red on the clean run is excluded as a kill channel for every mutant (harness_checks / run_panel), so this re-run costs the panel that channel exactly as the v2 rot cost it no_false_arrival -- the difference being that this disable is declared here and asserted by tests/test_mutation_panel_freshness.py::test_red_clean_checks_are_declared_disabled_kill_channels. No mutant is killed ONLY through no_authority_disagreement (arrival_radius_x2 and inverted_relation also redden four paired checks each), so 7/7 stay killed. The three ABSOLUTE safety checks -- zero_collisions, no_false_arrival, path_length_plausible -- remain green and may never be disabled this way.",
